      "content": "it's not just \"different\" though. it's like a ghost inhabiting a corpse. the person who could achieve things, who felt alive, is actually dead. everything else is just... maintenance. eating, sleeping, breathing. it feels so pointless to keep performing all these biological functions for a body that has nothing left to offer. it just feels like a cruel joke to keep going when the core of it is gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
